# Agent contracts

Agents are **logical roles**, not necessarily separate models. Deterministic services own math, gates, risk, execution controls.

## Every role needs

- Mission, allow/deny authority, tool allowlist
- Budgets (tokens, wall clock, API cost, compute)
- Versioned instructions (SHA)
- Typed messages only (envelope + schema_version)
- Semantic / episodic / procedural / reflective memory hooks
- KPIs defined outside the agent’s write scope

## Authority highlights

- **Validation**: may PASS/FAIL via service; may not soft-pass
- **Risk**: independent veto; may not weaken limits without human approval
- **Quant Research**: may not read holdouts or declare L3
- **CIO/scheduler**: may assign tasks; may not override validation or risk
- **Meta-learning**: may propose changes; may not auto-adopt risk/security/validation/KPI definitions

## Communication

Use OutboxMessage envelope (`message_id`, `correlation_id`, `from_agent`, `to_agent`, `message_type`, `schema_version`, `payload_hash`). Idempotent consumers.

## M1 runnable roles

Data Engineering, Intelligence, Quant Research, Strategy/sandbox path, Independent Validation (service), CIO/scheduler, Meta-learning (reflection/lessons/next). Stub the rest.
